{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "I'm Comin' Over feels like a natural continuation of my interest in 747 and Golden, so I would try it now; Ultimate Country Super Hits also interests me, although I would check the songs first.",
    "Amazing Grace suggests the reflective mood I enjoy in relaxing classical and expressive vocal recordings, making it an appealing possibility even though the title alone does not establish its sound."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The rock-focused choices and upbeat pop feel less suited to my current mood than the orchestral, relaxing, and expressive vocal recordings in my history.",
    "Titles such as Hits and A Collection Greatest Hits...And More give me no clear connection to an artist or songs I enjoy; being a collection is not enough to make me choose one."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My interest in some country albums seems to have been extended into a broader appetite for country collections, although the particular songs still matter to me.",
    "The repeated greatest-hits choices suggest that familiar-song collections were treated as appealing in themselves, while I need a connection to the voices, music, or mood I enjoy."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My most recent interaction with The Most Relaxing Classical Music in the Universe points toward calm listening, which few of these choices clearly offer.",
    "My repeated interest in Downton Abbey music, Stages, and vocal recordings suggests that expressive singing and orchestral atmosphere matter alongside my interest in country."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations picked up my interest in country but gave too little weight to my current preference for calm, expressive vocal and orchestral music."
}"}
